          "jcr:created": "Fri Feb 23 2024 14:14:56 GMT+0000",
          "text": "<h2><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">ComfortGel at a glance</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">The ComfortGel Support Surface is designed to redistribute pressure in the vulnerable sacral region to help prevent pressure injuries and provide optimal comfort for a superior patient experience.*</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">CoreGel</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Sloped heel</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Positioning pocket</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Immersion</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p>* The 84” ComfortGel Support Surface was used for the pressure mapping tests</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Fri Feb 23 2024 14:15:39 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
